Package: gtk4sermo
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, libgtk-4-1 (>= 4.6), libvte-2.91-gtk4-0
Conflicts: gtk4dialog
Replaces: gtk4dialog
Description: GTK 4 dialog boxes for shell scripts (gtkdialog successor)
 gtk4sermo builds native GTK 4 windows from an XML description, so a shell
 script can show a real graphical interface without any toolkit knowledge.
 .
 It is a maintained, hardened fork of gtkdialog (Laszlo Pere, Thunor) and reads
 the same XML as the GTK 3 port: existing gtkdialog scripts run unchanged.
 50 widgets, including GTK 4 natives — stack, revealer, flowbox, overlay,
 drawingarea — and client-side decorations.
 .
 Hardening: safe_exec (no system()), FORTIFY_SOURCE=3, PIE, Full RELRO,
 stack-protector-strong.
 .
 Part of the haplo-dialog suite, alongside gtk3sermo (GTK 3). Both install
 side by side: neither owns the gtkdialog command, which lives in the separate
 gtksermo package.
 .
 Drop-in replacement for gtkdialog: same XML language, same command-line
 interface — verified against a 55-case test corpus.
 .
 Not to be confused with the gtk3dialog package distributed by BunsenLabs,
 which is a different fork of the same ancestor.
